WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:25.820
Today’s protagonist was one of the key players
on the giant chessboard that was Asia at the

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:27.269
height of the Cold War.

00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:31.179
Born into a political family, she rose through
India’s political system until she became

00:00:31.179 --> 00:00:34.530
the first and only female Prime Minister of
her country.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.300
Her name was Indira Gandhi.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.791
In one of her speeches, she advised her followers
to maintain a ‘bias toward action,’ or

00:00:41.791 --> 00:00:47.130
to encourage societal change, even if required
painstakingly small steps.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:51.890
Her life was definitely true to that principle:
as the second longest-running Indian Prime

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:56.629
Minister, Mrs. Gandhi won a war, oversaw the
birth of a new State, broke the traditional

00:00:56.629 --> 00:01:02.219
non-aligned stance of India, and even made
of her country a nuclear super-power.

00:01:02.219 --> 00:01:07.590
But it was her internal policies that made
her mandate controversial, and eventually

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:10.430
turned her into a target of hatred.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:14.570
Welcome to today’s Biographics, in which
we will look at the private and public life

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:19.610
of Indira Gandhi, and how it all led to a
fateful appointment with the very people who

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.950
were meant to protect her.

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:30.010
Setting a good example
Indira Gandhi was born Indira Nehru on the

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:35.360
November 19th, 1917, in Allahabad, in the
state of Uttar Pradesh, India.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.290
She was the first-born child of Kamala and
Jawaharlal Nehru, who were no ordinary family.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:45.280
Kamala came from a conservative family of
Kashmiri Brahmins -- the category of priests

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.350
and teachers, according to the traditional
Indian caste system.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:54.140
This initially shy girl became an independence
activist after meeting her future husband,

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:55.420
Jawaharlal Nehru.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:02:00.810
Nehru was a well-educated lawyer and one of
the most active members of the Indian Independence

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:03.530
Movement, fighting for self-rule against the
British Empire.

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:08.341
As such, he was a close associate to the Mahatma
Gandhi, and would later serve as the first

00:02:08.341 --> 00:02:10.450
Prime Minister of an independent India.

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:15.470
While Nehru and Gandhi’s fight for independence
through non-cooperation is widely known, Kamala’s

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:17.640
role may have been overlooked.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:22.230
Beginning in 1921, Kamala was actively involved
in the Non-Cooperation movement, organising

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:26.150
boycotts and picketing lines against shops
selling British goods.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:30.500
When her husband was jailed by the colonial
authorities, Kamala shed her natural shyness

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.520
to deliver speeches to thousands of followers
on his behalf.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:39.300
With such fierce examples set by both her
parents, it is no wonder that little Indira

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.550
wanted to join the active struggle as early
as possible.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:47.370
At age five, she carried out her first act
of rebellion: she sacrificed her beloved doll

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:51.900
– made in England – by throwing it onto
a bonfire of imported British goods.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:57.500
Two years later, in 1924, the Nehru family
welcomed a second child, a boy, also born

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:58.500
in November.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:04.100
Unfortunately, the newborn died after only
two days, and Indira grew up as an only child.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:07.720
In 1929, she escalated her commitment to the
cause of self-determination.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:12.940
As a girl of only 12, Indira became a leader
within an organisation numbering 60,000 young

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:16.670
revolutionaries, called Vanar Sena, or ‘Monkey
Brigade’.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:21.000
This name was inspired by the traditional
epic Ramayana, in which an army of monkeys

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.990
helps Prince Rama to defeat the despotic and
monstrous Ravana.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:29.940
The Vanar Sena’s mission was less bellicose,
but still dangerous, as it involved managing

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:34.560
the communications and logistics that powered
mass demonstrations and protests.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:40.870
In March 1930, Indira and Kamala were participating
in one of such protests outside Ewing Christian

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:42.340
College in Allahabad.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:45.590
Indira's mother suddenly collapsed, due to
a heat stroke.

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:48.490
An eighteen-year old student of the College
rushed to her aid.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:51.590
His name was Feroz Gandhi -- no relation to
the Mahatma.

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:56.849
This chance encounter would prove one the
most important for Indira’s life so far.

00:03:56.849 --> 00:04:00.410
Feroz became a good friend of both Indira
and her mother, even helping to look after

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:03.270
Kamala when she later contracted tuberculosis.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:08.401
By 1936, Kamala moved to Switzerland to treat
her tuberculosis, but this was in vain: she

00:04:08.401 --> 00:04:13.410
passed away on February 28, 1936, while her
husband was in prison.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:17.220
Shortly after her mother’s death, Indira
traveled to Britain to enroll at Somerville

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:19.459
College in Oxford to complete her studies.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:24.169
She never attained a degree, though, as her
concentration may have been swayed by a big

00:04:24.169 --> 00:04:28.630
distraction, one that happened to be studying
at the nearby London School of Economics:

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:30.300
Feroz Gandhi.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:38.060
Mrs and Mr Gandhi
Indira and Feroz rekindled their friendship,

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:41.430
which turned into a courtship, and then into
an engagement.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:45.910
Like Indira, Feroz was also well-educated
involved in the independence movement, and

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:46.970
he loved Indira.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:51.210
Despite all this, his potential father-in-law
Nehru, objected to the union.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:55.710
Nehru simply had a personal dislike of the
young Gandhi, and as father of the bride,

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.630
he was entitled to a powerful opinion.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:02.470
As the Nehrus were a family under the spotlight,
many ordinary citizens also chipped in to

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:08.000
criticise the engagement, on the basis that
he was a Parsi, not a Hindu like Indira, or

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.440
that non-arranged marriages were not the norm.

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:15.210
In fact, there was such a public outcry against
the match that the other Gandhi, the Mahatma,

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:18.760
had to offer a public statement of support,
which included the request:

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:23.590
"I invite the writers of abusive letters to
shed your wrath and bless the forthcoming

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:24.590
marriage."

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:29.199
Despite the objections and the abuse, Indira
taught everybody a lesson in determination

00:05:29.199 --> 00:05:32.639
by marrying Feroz on March 26, 1942.

00:05:32.639 --> 00:05:38.699
Two years later, Indira gave birth to her
first son Rajiv, followed in 1946 by Sanjay.

00:05:38.699 --> 00:05:41.170
Unfortunately, this marriage was not a happy
one.

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:44.320
Feroz began having extramarital affairs almost
immediately.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:48.080
Things only got worse after August 15, 1947.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:52.990
This is the date in which Nehru became the
first Prime Minister of an independent India,

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:56.270
to which he added the title of Foreign Minister
in the October of the same year.

00:05:56.270 --> 00:06:01.639
In this capacity, Nehru handled the first
of many crises over Kashmir, a border region

00:06:01.639 --> 00:06:03.140
disputed with Pakistan.

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:08.540
As work kept on piling up on Nehru’s desk,
he enlisted his daughter Indira to help as

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:09.830
his personal assistant.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:14.110
This was an unofficial role, although it became
apparent to him and to the leadership of his

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:19.880
party – the Indian National Congress, or
INC – that Indira’s contribution was key

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:21.820
to carrying out his functions.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:25.690
Indira was spending more and more time with
his father’s cabinet, eventually moving

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:29.040
away from her hometown of Allahabad to the
capital, Delhi.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:34.620
Her two sons followed her, while Feroz decided
to stay back to concentrate on his work editing

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:40.020
‘The National Herald’ … but this arrangement
also gave him free rein to pursue more clandestine

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:41.400
liaisons.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:45.950
During this de facto separation, Indira appeared
to be completely absorbed by her administerial

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:47.470
and political duties.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:52.470
This is probably the truth; however, we should
mention that a book published in 1978 presents

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:53.800
a different image.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:07:00.300
This is the autobiography of M.O.Mathai, Private
Secretary to Prime Minister Nehru from 1946

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:01.520
to 1959.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:06.660
The 28th chapter, titled ‘She,’ was removed
from the final edition, but it has recently

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:09.290
re-emerged thanks to Indian online media.

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:14.500
According to the chapter, Indira tried to
seduce Mathai in November 1947, and quite

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:15.770
aggressively so.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:20.251
He yielded the day after, but due to being
completely inexperienced, Indira had to first

00:07:20.251 --> 00:07:24.460
‘educate’ him by giving him two books
about sex and the female anatomy.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:28.660
The chapter alleges that the clandestine relationship
continued for more than 10 years, until the

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:30.210
winter of 1958.

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:35.820
While visiting Indira on urgent official business,
Mathai caught her with another man, a yoga

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:36.820
instructor.

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:41.220
This chapter may have not even been written
by Mathai, and even if it were, Indira’s

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:43.960
close associates strongly refuted these rumours.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:47.770
According to a former leader of the Indian
National Congress, Natwar Singh, it would

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:53.680
have been materially impossible for Indira
to carry out some dangerous liaisons.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:56.479
According to Singh,
“It was just not possible for her to have

00:07:56.479 --> 00:07:59.070
an affair, there were security men under the
bed!

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:03.320
… Of course, you’re not made of wood but
this is the price you pay – you don’t

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:04.320
have a private life.”

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:12.850
First Steps on the Political Scene
Despite their marital issues, the Gandhis

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:15.840
presented a united front in the arena of Indian
politics.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:22.150
During the Parliamentary Elections in 1951-52,
Indira became the campaign manager for Feroz.

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:26.700
Indira clearly had a knack for campaigning
and succeeded in securing a victory for her

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:27.700
husband.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:31.860
After starting to serve as an MP, Feroz had
to move to Delhi, but he did not join his

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.199
family, preferring to live in a separate house.

00:08:34.199 --> 00:08:38.449
From then on, both Gandhis made their bid
to grow in status within the ruling party,

00:08:38.449 --> 00:08:42.699
the Indian National Congress, although admittedly
in two very different fashions.

00:08:42.699 --> 00:08:46.860
Feroz did so by exposing the corruption within
his father-in-law’s government.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:51.089
He exposed a major scandal involving bribes
paid by prominent insurance companies to the

00:08:51.089 --> 00:08:53.990
Finance Minister T.T. Krishnamachari.

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:58.329
Because of this, Feroz began to emerge as
the new rising star within India’s political

00:08:58.329 --> 00:08:59.329
circles.

00:08:59.329 --> 00:09:02.769
On the other hand, Indira was following another
route, rising from the inside of the INC party’s

00:09:02.769 --> 00:09:03.769
structure.

00:09:03.769 --> 00:09:09.089
In 1955, Indira first became a member, and
then a president, of the working committee

00:09:09.089 --> 00:09:13.870
of the Indian National Congress -- the inner
circle that decided the party’s policies.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:18.110
In 1958, Feroz suffered a heart attack during
a state visit to Bhutan.

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:21.769
Indira rushed him back to Delhi and took care
of him for the following year.

00:09:21.769 --> 00:09:26.809
She still managed to advance her career within
the party, and in 1959, Indira became President

00:09:26.809 --> 00:09:28.899
of the Indian National Congress.

00:09:28.899 --> 00:09:33.709
Marred by poor health, Feroz could not match
her rise, On the September 8, 1960, he suffered

00:09:33.709 --> 00:09:35.310
another cardiac arrest.

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:36.879
This time, it was fatal.

00:09:36.879 --> 00:09:39.990
The marriage of Indira and Feroz had not been
the happiest.

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:45.199
In addition to affairs and long periods of
separation, their life was marred by frequent,

00:09:45.199 --> 00:09:46.449
vicious arguments.

00:09:46.449 --> 00:09:50.819
According to Indira’s biographer Sagarika
Ghose, this was because both were extreme

00:09:50.819 --> 00:09:53.810
individualist, with an urge to dominate the
other.

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:56.860
And yet Indira remembered those confrontations
with fondness:

00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:02.389
“I like to think that those quarrels enlivened
our life, because without them, we would have

00:10:02.389 --> 00:10:05.290
had a normal life but banal and boring.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:10.069
We didn’t deserve a normal banal and boring
life.”

00:10:10.069 --> 00:10:16.790
Taking Centre Stage
Shortly after the death of Indira’s husband,

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.690
her father’s health began declining.

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:24.019
It did not help that in July 1962, India and
China entered a War over some border disputes,

00:10:24.019 --> 00:10:26.480
which ended with a Chinese victory in November.

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:31.759
Nehru’s conditions worsened, leading to
his death on May 27, 1964.

00:10:31.759 --> 00:10:37.410
Nehru was succeeded as Prime Minister by Lal
Bahadur Shastri, who appointed Indira as Minister

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:39.160
of Information and Broadcasting.

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:44.389
As a Minister, Indira proved very adept at
building her image with well-planned publicity

00:10:44.389 --> 00:10:49.410
stunts, such as the one taking place during
the Indo-Pakistani War of 1965.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:53.459
This confrontation over the control of the
Kashmir border region took place from the

00:10:53.459 --> 00:10:59.600
5th of August to the 22nd of September in
1965, when a UN resolution finally imposed

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:00.600
a ceasefire.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:03.709
That summer, Indira planned a holiday retreat
at Srinagar, in Kashmir.

00:11:03.709 --> 00:11:07.730
Despite repeated warnings by the security
forces that Pakistani troops had advanced

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:11.149
very close to her hotel, Indira Gandhi refused
to move.

00:11:11.149 --> 00:11:14.990
The incident fetched her huge national and
international media attention.

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:19.699
It would take only a few months for Indira
to take a role at the centre of the stage.

00:11:19.699 --> 00:11:23.100
On the 11th of January 1966, Prime Minister
Shastri died.

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:27.850
Immediately, his fellow party members began
squabbling and plotting to appoint a successor.

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:32.569
The leadership of the Indian National Congress
was by then split into two currents, one more

00:11:32.569 --> 00:11:35.699
conservative, the other with socialist leanings.

00:11:35.699 --> 00:11:39.629
These divisions made them unable to settle
on a candidate, and so they started considering

00:11:39.629 --> 00:11:41.339
an appointment for Indira Gandhi.

00:11:41.339 --> 00:11:45.170
They had been led to believe that she was
a goongi Gudiya, or ‘dumb doll’, easily

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:46.170
manipulated.

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:47.489
The perfect compromise candidate, then!

00:11:47.489 --> 00:11:51.929
After much deliberation, Indira was chosen
as the Prime Ministerial candidate by the

00:11:51.929 --> 00:11:53.420
Congress high command.

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:58.629
Indira campaigned hard and emerged victorious
on January 24, 1966.

00:11:58.629 --> 00:12:03.230
At the age of 49, Indira Gandhi had become
the Prime Minister of one of the largest and

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:05.509
most populous countries on Earth.

00:12:05.509 --> 00:12:10.040
She was not the first ever woman to be elected
head of state or head of government; in fact

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.329
she was only the third.

00:12:11.329 --> 00:12:15.160
The honour to be the first belongs to Khertek
Anchimaa, Chairwoman of the Tuvan’s People

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:17.440
Republic, from 1940 to 1944.

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:21.000
The country was annexed by the USSR and does
not exist anymore.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:25.730
The first-elected Prime Minister of a still
existing country was Sirimavo Bandaranaike:

00:12:25.730 --> 00:12:31.139
in 1960, she became the head of Government
in Sri Lanka, back then called Ceylon.

00:12:31.139 --> 00:12:36.179
So, Mrs Gandhi may have not set a record in
terms of timing, but she could wield an amount

00:12:36.179 --> 00:12:39.429
of power that her predecessors definitely
could not boast.

00:12:39.429 --> 00:13:19.329
And that power was just about

00:13:19.329 --> 00:13:27.769
to increase.

00:13:27.769 --> 00:13:51.970
From Strength to Strength
When Mrs. Gandhi was elected, the INC party

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:54.290
was split in two opposing factions.

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:57.529
Of the two, Indira sided with the socialist-leaning
one.

00:13:57.529 --> 00:14:02.810
The INC was further weakened when new parliamentary
elections took place in 1967, and the party

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:04.869
lost 60 seats in the lower house.

00:14:04.869 --> 00:14:09.929
In normal situations, this landslide defeat
would spell the fall of the cabinet in charge.

00:14:09.929 --> 00:14:13.189
But the person in charge of the cabinet was
not your normal Prime Minister.

00:14:13.189 --> 00:14:17.629
Indira Gandhi proved that her tenacity to
cling to power was unparalleled.

00:14:17.629 --> 00:14:22.329
In order to ensure the survival of her government,
Mrs. Gandhi went as far as forging a coalition

00:14:22.329 --> 00:14:26.649
with the Socialist and Communist Parties,
something unthinkable a few years earlier,

00:14:26.649 --> 00:14:28.660
during her father Jawaharlal’s term in office.

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:31.109
Why do I say unthinkable?

00:14:31.109 --> 00:14:35.689
Nehru may have had a moderate interest in
socialist political and economic reform, but

00:14:35.689 --> 00:14:40.800
in the context of the Cold War he definitely
avoided siding with the Socialist Bloc.

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:43.899
Nor with the Capitalist Bloc, for that matter.

00:14:43.899 --> 00:14:49.389
Nehru, alongside Egypt’s Nasser and Yugolsavia’s
Tito, was one of the key leaders of the ‘non-aligned’

00:14:49.389 --> 00:14:50.389
countries.

00:14:50.389 --> 00:14:54.550
While the world debated capitalism versus
communism, India was mostly uninterested in

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:55.720
taking a side.

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:59.310
Now, though, Nehru’s daughter and successor,
far from being an easily swayed ‘doll’,

00:14:59.310 --> 00:15:04.189
was taking decisive action to steer India
into a much clearer Socialist direction.

00:15:04.189 --> 00:15:09.339
Domestically, in 1969, Mrs Gandhi’s cabinet
nationalised the fourteen largest banks in

00:15:09.339 --> 00:15:12.579
India, as well as the four most important
oil companies.

00:15:12.579 --> 00:15:17.180
Other reforms included the abolition of privileges
for the Maharajas, who still held power in

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:18.820
several of India’s States.

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:23.749
Finally, Mrs. Gandhi initiated an agricultural
reform based on the Green Revolution concepts

00:15:23.749 --> 00:15:28.749
developed by US Scientist Norman Borlaug:
a combination of mechanised agriculture and

00:15:28.749 --> 00:15:31.489
development of new breeds of high-yield plants.

00:15:31.489 --> 00:15:36.000
Thanks to Gandhi’s reforms, India, normally
beset by periodic famines, became an exporter

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:37.720
of surplus rice and wheat.

00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:42.160
As far as foreign policy goes, Indira Gandhi’s
time in office was marked by tension and outright

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:45.040
hostility toward China, Pakistan, and the
US.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:49.800
At the same time, India signed a Peace, Friendship
and Cooperation treaty with the Soviet Union

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:55.480
in August 1971, marking a further drift away
from equidistant non-alignment and towards

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:56.490
the Socialist Bloc.

00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:58.639
But let’s proceed in order.

00:15:58.639 --> 00:16:04.079
The enmity with China dated back from the
1962 war and was exacerbated by Beijing’s

00:16:04.079 --> 00:16:05.920
nuclear tests in 1967.

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:10.029
The shadow of this atomic threat prompted
Gandhi to start pursuing India’s own nuclear

00:16:10.029 --> 00:16:11.029
program.

00:16:11.029 --> 00:16:14.549
Within just seven years, the country was able
to perform their first underground detonation.

00:16:14.549 --> 00:16:19.910
The rivalry with Pakistan over Kashmir was
as old as India’s independence and had resulted

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:21.689
already in two border wars.

00:16:21.689 --> 00:16:25.299
The two countries were about to enter a further
conflict in 1971.

00:16:25.299 --> 00:16:31.040
At that time, Pakistan was split into two
separate territories, East and West Pakistan,

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:32.459
separated by Northern India.

00:16:32.459 --> 00:16:36.689
Islamabad’s armed forces launched a violent
counter-insurgency campaign in the Eastern

00:16:36.689 --> 00:16:40.459
half to suppress the Awami League, an independentist
movement.

00:16:40.459 --> 00:16:44.989
The result of this internal struggle was that
about 10 million East Pakistani citizens fled

00:16:44.989 --> 00:16:46.569
into India as refugees.

00:16:46.569 --> 00:16:51.809
The unprecedented humanitarian crisis stretched
India’s resource to the limit, and it prompted

00:16:51.809 --> 00:16:56.389
Indira Gandhi to harshly condemn the repression
on the 31st of March.

00:16:56.389 --> 00:17:00.769
Soon, she started doing something more than
just speaking sternly -- Indira started supporting

00:17:00.769 --> 00:17:03.149
the Awami League in their independence fight.

00:17:03.149 --> 00:17:07.790
This was effectively a war by proxy against
Pakistan, a calculated move to weaken the

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:12.140
hostile neighbour and create a friendlier
government on the North Eastern border.

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:17.690
Toward the end of the year, this local conflict
took on regional, then international connotations.

00:17:17.690 --> 00:17:20.650
To put it simply
Pakistan did not like India.

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:21.829
China did not like India.

00:17:21.829 --> 00:17:24.030
So, China supported Pakistan.

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:26.000
Enter a new player: the US.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:29.891
China and the Soviet Union were not best pals
anymore, so Nixon sought a rapprochement with

00:17:29.891 --> 00:17:30.891
Mao.

00:17:30.891 --> 00:17:33.630
Ergo: the US liked China, who liked Pakistan.

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:37.190
The US planned to help Pakistan, should India
declare war.

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:39.900
All this implies that:
If China dislikes India, and

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:44.330
If the US dislike India,
India is going to make friends with a country

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:47.890
those two also dislike: the Soviet Union.

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:51.460
Hence the Peace, Friendship and Cooperation
treaty I mentioned earlier!

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:57.350
In December of 1971, the conflict by proxy
against Pakistan became a full-fledged war.

00:17:57.350 --> 00:18:01.420
On the 3rd of December, Pakistan decided to
retaliate against India’s involvement with

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:07.010
the Awami League by bombing Indian air fields
in the western regions of Punjab and Kashmir.

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:11.860
The Indian government under Indira Gandhi
had proven able to take quick, decisive actions,

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:13.650
and the military was no different.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:18.130
The Indian air force retaliated on the 4th
and quickly achieved air superiority.

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:23.120
On the ground, the Army launched a quick attack
into East Pakistan, converging on the regional

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:24.120
capital, Dhaka.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:28.500
On the 9th of December, the war risked escalating
beyond the Indian subcontinent, when Nixon

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:31.280
ordered for a US fleet to head toward the
theater of action.

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:34.890
What may have happened, if the US provided
direct support to Pakistan?

00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:39.660
We will never know: by the 16th of December,
Dhaka had fallen to the Indian Army and the

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:41.970
separatist forces of the Awami League.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:46.510
The Indian victory in the third war with Pakistan
was a personal triumph for Indira Gandhi,

00:18:46.510 --> 00:18:51.760
and resulted in the birth of a new nation:
East Pakistan seceded and became Bangladesh.

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:55.080
After the peace had been signed, the Prime
Minister issued a clear warning in an interview

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:59.750
with media, to powers both foreign and domestic:
“I am not a person to be pressured — by

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:01.410
anybody or any nation."

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:10.630
State of Emergency
The 1970s had begun well for Mrs. Gandhi,

00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:12.750
and she would soon score another triumph.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:17.440
In 1972, the INC faced the Socialist Party
in national parliamentary elections.

00:19:17.440 --> 00:19:22.420
Gandhi’s party triumphed in the ballot boxes,
thanks to the recent victory over Pakistan

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:25.590
and to her campaign promise to eradicate poverty.

00:19:25.590 --> 00:19:30.550
The defeated Socialist leader, Raj Narain,
raised allegations of corruption and electoral

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:31.550
malpractice.

00:19:31.550 --> 00:19:35.790
Soon, Socialist and other opposition parties
took to the street, protesting against Gandhi’s

00:19:35.790 --> 00:19:36.790
government.

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:40.840
As the decade progressed, Gandhi’s economic
and social reform were largely nullified by

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:44.360
rising inflation and a generally poor state
of the economy.

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:47.240
All this only played in the hands of protesters.

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:52.530
Narain’s charges were formalised with the
High Court in Allahabad, who in June of 1975

00:19:52.530 --> 00:19:53.750
ruled against the Prime Minister.

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:57.700
Now Indira Gandhi was constitutionally expected
to step down from office.

00:19:57.700 --> 00:20:01.250
But she had already made it clear once: she
wasn’t going to be pressured by anybody.

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:05.520
As unrest spread throughout the country following
the court ruling, Mrs Gandhi took this as

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:10.200
the perfect occasion to declare a state of
emergency, giving her extraordinary powers

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:11.530
to rule by decree.

00:20:11.530 --> 00:20:15.820
The period of emergency rule lasted two years,
and it would be a black moment for Indian

00:20:15.820 --> 00:20:16.820
democracy.

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:21.010
The country became a dictatorship in all but
name: as an authoritarian ruler, Indira Gandhi

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:26.170
ordered political opponents and other activists
to be jailed, press freedom to be limited.

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:30.580
Indira’s main accomplice and confidante
was her second-born son, Sanjay.

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:34.580
Taking advantage of extraordinary powers,
Sanjay put into practice some pet projects

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:37.970
of his: first, the forced removal of slum
dwellings.

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:42.700
More importantly, India enacted population
control via forced sterilisation.

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:47.570
This draconian measure was considered a necessary
evil to allow for the country to prosper.

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:51.550
Indira’s government launched a campaign
of vasectomies, starting with public employees:

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:54.840
they were required to go through sterilisation
to receive their salaries.

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:58.860
The campaign was then extended to any male
citizen, who would be offered cash, or even

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:02.180
just cooking oil, as an incentive to accept
a vasectomy.

00:21:02.180 --> 00:21:06.220
Sanjay’s plans did not stop there: reports
came out that vasectomies had been performed

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:10.450
even on teenage boys, or that men were being
arrested and sterilized.

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:16.480
According to an exposé by TIME magazine,
between April 1976 and January 1977, 7.8 million

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:21.180
Indian boys and men were sterilized -- well
beyond the initial government target of 4.3

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:22.180
million.

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:26.310
At the beginning of 1977, Indira Gandhi put
an end to the state of emergency by calling

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:27.410
for new elections.

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:31.640
The Prime Minister thought that all opposition
had been effectively suppressed, and this

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:35.400
would have been an easy win, one to legitimise
her permanence in office.

00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:40.000
But I will take a guess here and say that
one half of the electorate was not too keen

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:41.000
on Gandhi.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:44.580
You know, the one half that doesn’t like
their manhood to be messed with by forced

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:48.060
surgery …
The elections resulted in a crushing defeat

00:21:48.060 --> 00:21:52.660
for the INC: they lost almost 200 seats compared
to the previous legislature.

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:56.920
The big winner this time was the Janata Dal,
or ‘People’s Party’, a coalition of

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:58.520
several smaller parties.

00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:03.170
Indira accepted defeat and stepped down.

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:09.520
Blue Star
Mrs Gandhi may have left office as Prime Minister,

00:22:09.520 --> 00:22:14.130
but she still held a seat in Parliament, from
which she led the opposition against the Janata

00:22:14.130 --> 00:22:15.130
Dal.

00:22:15.130 --> 00:22:19.160
The new government tried to remove her by
having her jailed briefly twice: in October

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:21.660
of 1977, and then again in December of 1978.

00:22:21.660 --> 00:22:25.030
In both occasions, the charges were corruption.

00:22:25.030 --> 00:22:26.510
But the plan did not work.

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:30.480
As the tenuous alliance within the Janata
started to crumble, the electorate called

00:22:30.480 --> 00:22:34.470
for stability – something that Indira and
the INC could guarantee.

00:22:34.470 --> 00:22:38.810
New elections were called in January 1980,
and Mrs Gandhi made a surprising come back

00:22:38.810 --> 00:22:40.120
as head of the Government.

00:22:40.120 --> 00:22:43.670
During the same elections, Indira’s son
Sanjay won a seat in parliament.

00:22:43.670 --> 00:22:48.750
By May, Mrs Gandhi made it clear that he was
her heir apparent by appointing him as secretary

00:22:48.750 --> 00:22:52.840
general of the INC.
Sanjay’s rise had to stop abruptly June

00:22:52.840 --> 00:22:53.840
23, 1980.

00:22:53.840 --> 00:22:58.340
For years Sanjay had been practising with
some success in the sport of aircraft aerobatics.

00:22:58.340 --> 00:23:00.660
That day, too, Sanjay had gone out flying.

00:23:00.660 --> 00:23:05.310
But while performing aerial loops, he lost
control and crashed with his plane, dying

00:23:05.310 --> 00:23:06.310
on the spot.

00:23:06.310 --> 00:23:10.520
Older brother Rajiv also had a passion for
flying; until then he had not shown any interest

00:23:10.520 --> 00:23:13.430
in politics, working as a commercial pilot
for Indian Airlines.

00:23:13.430 --> 00:23:17.660
But after this tragedy, Indira called him
back into the fold of family politics.

00:23:17.660 --> 00:23:22.080
It was clear that she was building the Nehru-Gandhi
dynastic line.

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:26.720
Indira expected the whole family to form a
united front behind Rajiv’s budding political

00:23:26.720 --> 00:23:29.710
career, including Maneka, Sanjay’s widow.

00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:34.140
But Indira and Maneka had never got on well,
and in 1982, a serious disagreement broke

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:35.340
out between the two.

00:23:35.340 --> 00:23:39.810
Maneka attended a rally held by Sanjay's former
political associates, which was perceived

00:23:39.810 --> 00:23:42.640
by the Prime Minister as a slight towards
Rajiv.

00:23:42.640 --> 00:23:46.680
Indira ordered Maneka to leave the house in
which the extended family all lived together.

00:23:46.680 --> 00:23:51.500
The daughter-in-law complied, but first she
made sure the press was aware of her unfair

00:23:51.500 --> 00:23:52.500
eviction.

00:23:52.500 --> 00:23:56.220
Then, she separated Indira from hers and Sanjay’s
son, Varun.

00:23:56.220 --> 00:23:59.180
Not being able to see her grandson was a hard
blow for the Prime Minister.

00:23:59.180 --> 00:24:03.560
As it turned out, it became one she could
not recover from, as public troubles piled

00:24:03.560 --> 00:24:05.310
on top of the private ones.

00:24:05.310 --> 00:24:10.240
By 1982, Mrs. Gandhi had to face the growth
of secessionist movements all over India.

00:24:10.240 --> 00:24:15.610
Unrest flared up in the regions of Andhra
Pradesh, Jammu and Kashmir, but the most serious

00:24:15.610 --> 00:24:20.520
threat came from the Sikh secessionist movement
in Punjab, Northwestern India.

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:25.720
The movement was led by Jarnail Singh Bhindranwale,
who opposed peaceful negotiations with the

00:24:25.720 --> 00:24:26.940
government in Delhi.

00:24:26.940 --> 00:24:30.940
In July of 1982, Bhindranwale established
his headquarters within the Harmandir Sahib,

00:24:30.940 --> 00:24:34.130
or Golden Temple, in Amritsar, Punjab.

00:24:34.130 --> 00:24:38.570
The Golden Temple is the most prominent centre
of worship and pilgrimage for the Sikh faith:

00:24:38.570 --> 00:24:42.660
within its walls, Bhindranwale began recruiting
supporters and amassing weapons for an armed

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:43.660
insurrection.

00:24:43.660 --> 00:24:48.050
Indira’s government grew more and more concerned
about the Sikh separatist intentions, so eventually,

00:24:48.050 --> 00:24:51.730
in February1984, the Prime Minister decided
to go on the offensive.

00:24:51.730 --> 00:24:56.500
The initial plan was to have airborne commandos
kidnap Bhindranwale, but this was aborted

00:24:56.500 --> 00:25:01.540
in favour of a large scale occupation of the
Golden Temple by Special Forces: ‘Operation

00:25:01.540 --> 00:25:02.650
Blue Star’.

00:25:02.650 --> 00:25:06.260
Blue Star launched on the night between the
5th and the 6th of June 1984.

00:25:06.260 --> 00:25:11.240
The besieged Sikhs answered with heavy fire,
including shooting RPGs at armoured vehicles,

00:25:11.240 --> 00:25:15.440
but after a night of fighting, the Indian
commandos seized the Akal Takhat building,

00:25:15.440 --> 00:25:18.240
in which Bhindranwale had staged his last
stand.

00:25:18.240 --> 00:25:22.761
The palace was hit by light arms fire, tank
shells, and tear gas canisters: by 6am on

00:25:22.761 --> 00:25:27.110
the 6th, resistance had ceased and Bhindranwale’s
body was discovered among the rubble.

00:25:27.110 --> 00:25:31.830
83 troops lost their lives in the assault,
versus 492 civilian fatalities.

00:25:31.830 --> 00:25:36.010
Some of these fatalities were Sikh separatists,
but most were civilians.

00:25:36.010 --> 00:25:40.250
The majority of the dead were pilgrims who
happened to be inside the temple at the wrong

00:25:40.250 --> 00:25:41.250
time.

00:25:41.250 --> 00:25:45.250
Operation Blue Star was followed by Operation
Woodrose, a larger military deployment which

00:25:45.250 --> 00:25:50.060
included infantry, armour, artillery, and
helicopters confronting Sikh independentists

00:25:50.060 --> 00:25:51.250
across all of Punjab.

00:25:51.250 --> 00:25:55.730
Both operations widened the rift between the
Sikh minority and the rest of the country.

00:25:55.730 --> 00:26:00.410
Indira Gandhi’s prestige and popularity,
which had made a recovery since the 1980 re-election,

00:26:00.410 --> 00:26:02.060
were heavily tarnished once again.

00:26:02.060 --> 00:26:06.780
But something much, much worse than a dip
in popularity was on the horizon for the Prime

00:26:06.780 --> 00:26:07.780
Minister.

00:26:07.780 --> 00:26:12.430
On the morning of October 31st, 1984, Indira
Gandhi was walking from her official residence

00:26:12.430 --> 00:26:17.130
toward her office to meet British actor Peter
Ustinov, who was there to interview her for

00:26:17.130 --> 00:26:18.550
a BBC documentary.

00:26:18.550 --> 00:26:22.950
She was walking a few paces ahead of her attendant,
as she approached the gates leading out of

00:26:22.950 --> 00:26:23.950
her gardens.

00:26:23.950 --> 00:26:27.960
At 9:09 am, Mrs Gandhi folded her hands to
greet the two bodyguards stationed at the

00:26:27.960 --> 00:26:31.360
gates, Beant Singh and Satwant Singh.

00:26:31.360 --> 00:26:32.890
These guards were not related.

00:26:32.890 --> 00:26:37.160
The Sanskrit word ‘Singh’ means lion,
and it is an essential component of all male

00:26:37.160 --> 00:26:38.670
names among the Sikhs.

00:26:38.670 --> 00:26:43.210
It was only four months since Operations Blue
Star and Woodrose, but the Prime Minister

00:26:43.210 --> 00:26:46.260
had no reason to mistrust her loyal Sikh bodyguards.

00:26:46.260 --> 00:26:51.060
In the case of Beant and Satwant, she had
made a mistake: the two had been planning

00:26:51.060 --> 00:26:53.570
their revenge for the massacre at the Golden
Temple.

00:26:53.570 --> 00:26:58.730
Beant fired the first shots with his revolver,
followed by Satwant, who fired his Sten submachine

00:26:58.730 --> 00:26:59.970
gun on full auto.

00:26:59.970 --> 00:27:01.790
Indira Gandhi was shot 30 times.

00:27:01.790 --> 00:27:06.670
She was rushed to a hospital, but her death
was announced at 1 pm the same day.

00:27:06.670 --> 00:27:11.470
The following day, ordinary citizens, in many
cases aided and supported by police and local

00:27:11.470 --> 00:27:16.500
authorities, started a series of violent anti-Sikh
riots, which resulted in the death of more

00:27:16.500 --> 00:27:18.430
than 3,000 Sikhs.

00:27:18.430 --> 00:27:25.250
The death of a leader had sparked a period
of unrest for her country – but that’s

00:27:25.250 --> 00:27:28.370
another story.

00:27:28.370 --> 00:27:31.820
Legacy
Indira Gandhi had built her political career

00:27:31.820 --> 00:27:35.620
on the principle of bold action, independent
from external pressure.

00:27:35.620 --> 00:27:40.980
This had led to successes like the Green revolution,
the victory against Pakistan, the alliance

00:27:40.980 --> 00:27:43.830
with the USSR, and a stable nuclear programme.

00:27:43.830 --> 00:27:48.770
Indira also succeeded in ensuring the continuation
of the Nehru/Gandhi dynasty.

00:27:48.770 --> 00:27:52.830
Shortly after the assassination, her son Rajiv
was sworn in as new Prime Minister.

00:27:52.830 --> 00:27:57.860
Rajiv remained in power for seven years, until
he, too, was assassinated in May 1991 by a

00:27:57.860 --> 00:28:02.460
suicide bomber from aSri Lankan militant group,
known as the ‘Tamil Tigers’.

00:28:02.460 --> 00:28:07.760
In 1997, Rajiv’s wife Sonia was elected
by INC members as their party President, a

00:28:07.760 --> 00:28:12.110
key role in setting the policies of the Country
. Sonia Gandhi could have easily won over

00:28:12.110 --> 00:28:13.420
the seat of Prime Minister.

00:28:13.420 --> 00:28:17.610
But the fact that she is Italian by birth,
did not allow her to cover official Government

00:28:17.610 --> 00:28:20.440
functions, let alone become the head of said
Government.

00:28:20.440 --> 00:28:25.630
In 2017, Sonia continued the Dynastic tradition
and handed over direction of the party to

00:28:25.630 --> 00:28:27.050
her son Rahul.

00:28:27.050 --> 00:28:32.240
However, this was the story of a strong leader,
and as usual, there are shadows behind the

00:28:32.240 --> 00:28:33.240
triumphs.

00:28:33.240 --> 00:28:38.250
It is not possible to overlook the excesses
of the emergency years, the allegations of

00:28:38.250 --> 00:28:44.140
corruption, the poor management of the economy
and finally the immediate and lasting effects

00:28:44.140 --> 00:29:00.710
of Operation Blue Star.

